# An extension attaches chrome.debugger, as the Playwright MCP bridge does, and Chrome shows its
# "<extension> started debugging this browser" bar above the page. The compositor drew the page
# below the bar, but the card laid the page's input view over the whole web area, so every click
# landed one bar-height low, and the bar's Cancel and ✕ took no clicks at all (GitHub #241).
# The input view keeps Chromium's place below the bar when the card lays out again, also after a
# resize, and a click on the bar's ✕ reaches Chrome's views: the bar goes and the page fills
# the card again.
# promise: #241
budget rss=700 stalls50=5
cra://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/DebuggerExtension
relaunch
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
wait 1
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=debugger
expect-log page view: Chromium insets top=[1-9][0-9]* left=0 bottom=0 right=0
wait 1
cra://debug?pageInsets=1
expect-log page view insets 1: top=[1-9][0-9]* left=0 bottom=0 right=0; Chromium's top=[1-9]
cra://debug?windowSize=1000x700
wait 1
cra://debug?pageInsets=1
expect-log page view insets 2: top=[1-9][0-9]* left=0 bottom=0 right=0; Chromium's top=[1-9]
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
wait 1
# The bar's ✕, 20 pt in from the page's right edge (the page area spans x 328…1190 from y 10).
cra://debug?clickAt=1170,38
expect-log page view: Chromium insets top=0 left=0 bottom=0 right=0
wait 1
cra://debug?pageInsets=1
expect-log page view insets 3: top=0 left=0 bottom=0 right=0; Chromium's top=0
reject-log fault:
